IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P1-art-6b.l4 -- ARTICLE 6(3) AND (4).  Layer 1 (P1).
-- 6(3): what the legal basis for points (c) and (e) of Art 6(1) must be; 6(4): what the controller must
-- weigh before processing for another purpose.
-- Whose duty: 6(3) binds the lawmaker (an official: encoded for what it means to the controller and
-- the data subject: whether the processing has a valid legal basis); 6(4) binds the controller.
-- Borrowed: Art 23(1) objectives (P2), "necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society".
-- ============================================================================

§ `Article 6(3): the legal basis for points (c) and (e)`

-- src:97 | 3. The basis for the processing referred to in point (c) and (e) of paragraph 1 shall be laid down by:
-- src:98 | (a) Union law; or
-- src:99 | (b) Member State law to which the controller is subject.
@ref Art 6(3)(a) and (b) (src:97-99)
GIVEN `the basis of the processing` IS AN `Art 6(1) lawful basis`
      `the basis is laid down by Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the basis is laid down by Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller is subject to that Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(3) the basis for the processing is laid down by Union law or by Member State law to which the controller is subject` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (    `the basis of the processing` EQUALS `Art 6(1)(c) legal obligation`
                OR `the basis of the processing` EQUALS `Art 6(1)(e) public interest or official authority`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The basis for the processing referred to in point (c) and (e) of paragraph 1"; the other four bases are not spoken of
        IF `the basis is laid down by Union law`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the basis is laid down by Member State law` AND `the controller is subject to that Member State law`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "shall be laid down by: (a) Union law; or (b) Member State law to which the controller is subject"

-- src:100 | The purpose of the processing shall be determined in that legal basis or, as regards the processing referred to in point (e) of paragraph 1, shall be necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller. That legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of rules of this Regulation, inter alia: the general conditions governing the lawfulness of processing by the controller; the types of data which are subject to the processing; the data subjects concerned; the entities to, and the purposes for which, the personal data may be disclosed; the purpose limitation; storage periods; and processing operations and processing procedures, including measures to ensure lawful and fair processing such as those for other specific processing situations as provided for in Chapter IX. The Union or the Member State law shall meet an objective of public interest and be proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued.
@ref Art 6(3), second paragraph, first sentence (src:100)
GIVEN `the basis of the processing` IS AN `Art 6(1) lawful basis`
      `the purpose of the processing is determined in that legal basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(3) the purpose of the processing is determined in the legal basis or, for point (e), is necessary for the task` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (    `the basis of the processing` EQUALS `Art 6(1)(c) legal obligation`
                OR `the basis of the processing` EQUALS `Art 6(1)(e) public interest or official authority`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that legal basis" is the basis "referred to in point (c) and (e)"
        IF `the purpose of the processing is determined in that legal basis`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the basis of the processing` EQUALS `Art 6(1)(e) public interest or official authority`
           AND `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "The purpose of the processing shall be determined in that legal basis or, as regards the processing referred to in point (e) of paragraph 1, shall be necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller."

DECLARE `Art 6(3) matter a legal basis may adapt` IS ONE OF
    `Art 6(3) the general conditions governing the lawfulness of processing by the controller`
    `Art 6(3) the types of data which are subject to the processing`
    `Art 6(3) the data subjects concerned`
    `Art 6(3) the entities to which the personal data may be disclosed`
    `Art 6(3) the purposes for which the personal data may be disclosed`
    `Art 6(3) the purpose limitation`
    `Art 6(3) storage periods`
    `Art 6(3) processing operations and processing procedures, including measures to ensure lawful and fair processing`
    `Art 6(3) some other matter`

-- src:100 | The purpose of the processing shall be determined in that legal basis or, as regards the processing referred to in point (e) of paragraph 1, shall be necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller. That legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of rules of this Regulation, inter alia: the general conditions governing the lawfulness of processing by the controller; the types of data which are subject to the processing; the data subjects concerned; the entities to, and the purposes for which, the personal data may be disclosed; the purpose limitation; storage periods; and processing operations and processing procedures, including measures to ensure lawful and fair processing such as those for other specific processing situations as provided for in Chapter IX. The Union or the Member State law shall meet an objective of public interest and be proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued.
@ref Art 6(3), second paragraph, second sentence (src:100)
GIVEN matter IS AN `Art 6(3) matter a legal basis may adapt`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(3) the legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of the rules of this Regulation on the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT (matter EQUALS `Art 6(3) some other matter`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "inter alia" introduces the list, so a matter the list does not name is neither permitted nor excluded

-- src:100 | The purpose of the processing shall be determined in that legal basis or, as regards the processing referred to in point (e) of paragraph 1, shall be necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller. That legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of rules of this Regulation, inter alia: the general conditions governing the lawfulness of processing by the controller; the types of data which are subject to the processing; the data subjects concerned; the entities to, and the purposes for which, the personal data may be disclosed; the purpose limitation; storage periods; and processing operations and processing procedures, including measures to ensure lawful and fair processing such as those for other specific processing situations as provided for in Chapter IX. The Union or the Member State law shall meet an objective of public interest and be proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued.
@ref Art 6(3), second paragraph, last sentence (src:100)
GIVEN `the law meets an objective of public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law is proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(3) the Union or Member State law meets an objective of public interest and is proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued` MEANS
    IF `the law meets an objective of public interest` AND `the law is proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "The Union or the Member State law shall meet an objective of public interest and be proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued."

§ `Article 6(4): processing for another purpose`

DECLARE `Art 6(4) matter to be taken into account` IS ONE OF
    `Art 6(4)(a) any link between the purposes`
    `Art 6(4)(b) the context in which the personal data have been collected`
    `Art 6(4)(c) the nature of the personal data`
    `Art 6(4)(d) the possible consequences of the intended further processing for data subjects`
    `Art 6(4)(e) the existence of appropriate safeguards`
    `Art 6(4) some other matter`

DECLARE `Art 6(4) action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 6(4) take into account the matters (a) to (e) to ascertain whether processing for another purpose is compatible`

-- src:101 | 4. Where the processing for a purpose other than that for which the personal data have been collected is not based on the data subject's consent or on a Union or Member State law which constitutes a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard the objectives referred to in Article 23(1), the controller shall, in order to ascertain whether processing for another purpose is compatible with the purpose for which the personal data are initially collected, take into account, inter alia:
-- src:102 | (a) any link between the purposes for which the personal data have been collected and the purposes of the intended further processing;
-- src:103 | (b) the context in which the personal data have been collected, in particular regarding the relationship between data subjects and the controller;
-- src:104 | (c) the nature of the personal data, in particular whether special categories of personal data are processed, pursuant to Article 9, or whether personal data related to criminal convictions and offences are processed, pursuant to Article 10;
-- src:105 | (d) the possible consequences of the intended further processing for data subjects;
-- src:106 | (e) the existence of appropriate safeguards, which may include encryption or pseudonymisation.
@ref Art 6(4) (src:101-106)
GIVEN `the processing is for a purpose other than that for which the personal data have been collected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is based on the data subject's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is based on a Union or Member State law which constitutes a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard the objectives referred to in Article 23(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matters the controller has taken into account` IS A LIST OF `Art 6(4) matter to be taken into account`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the processing is for a purpose other than that for which the personal data have been collected`)
           OR `the processing is based on the data subject's consent`
           OR `the processing is based on a Union or Member State law which constitutes a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard the objectives referred to in Article 23(1)`
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "Where"): "Where the processing for a purpose other than that for which the personal data have been collected is not based on the data subject's consent or on a Union or Member State law which constitutes a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard the objectives referred to in Article 23(1), the controller shall"
        IF     elem `Art 6(4)(a) any link between the purposes` `the matters the controller has taken into account`
           AND elem `Art 6(4)(b) the context in which the personal data have been collected` `the matters the controller has taken into account`
           AND elem `Art 6(4)(c) the nature of the personal data` `the matters the controller has taken into account`
           AND elem `Art 6(4)(d) the possible consequences of the intended further processing for data subjects` `the matters the controller has taken into account`
           AND elem `Art 6(4)(e) the existence of appropriate safeguards` `the matters the controller has taken into account`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        -- "inter alia": further matters beyond (a) to (e) are allowed and change nothing (the member `Art 6(4) some other matter`)
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "the controller shall, in order to ascertain whether processing for another purpose is compatible with the purpose for which the personal data are initially collected, take into account, inter alia: (a) ... (e)"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule.  The text names the party (the controller) and the act (take into
-- account) but states no time limit and no consequence: no trace can show it breached (NOTES.md).
@ref Art 6(4), regulative form (src:101-101)
GIVEN `the gate holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 6(4) action`
`Art 6(4) the controller must take into account the matters (a) to (e)` MEANS
    IF `the gate holds`
    THEN PARTY `controller`
         MUST `Art 6(4) take into account the matters (a) to (e) to ascertain whether processing for another purpose is compatible`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `Art 6(4) the controller must take into account the matters (a) to (e)` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `controller` DOES `Art 6(4) take into account the matters (a) to (e) to ascertain whether processing for another purpose is compatible` AT 5
-- Result on the main build: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `Art 6(4) the controller must take into account the matters (a) to (e)` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
-- Result on the main build: the obligation is still standing (no deadline in the text, so no breach).
#TRACE `Art 6(4) the controller must take into account the matters (a) to (e)` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
-- Result on the main build: FULFILLED (the gate "Where ..." does not hold, so there is no duty).
